    <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Outbound is made by edbnme ("we", "us"). We decide how the personal data described here is used, which makes us its controller under the GDPR and UK GDPR, the business under U.S. state privacy laws, and the data fiduciary under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, where those laws apply.</li>
      <li>On this website, Outbound is sold by our reseller Polar, and on the Mac App Store by Apple. Each handles the payment details it collects under its own privacy policy, as described in sections <a href="#app-store">3</a> and <a href="#buying">7</a>.</li>
      <li>This policy covers the Outbound app, from this website or the Mac App Store, and the website at outbound.edbn.me.</li>
      <li>Write to <a href="mailto:outbound@edbn.me">outbound@edbn.me</a> about anything here. We haven't appointed a data protection officer, as we aren't required to; that address reaches the person who makes Outbound.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="short">2. In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The app collects nothing about you or how you use it. No analytics, ads, tracking or crash reports.</li>
      <li>The copy from the Mac App Store makes no network requests at all.</li>
      <li>The copy from this website goes online only to check its license and to look for updates.</li>
      <li>This website counts visits with Plausible, which sets no cookies and keeps nothing that identifies you.</li>
      <li>Payments are taken by Polar on this website, and by Apple on the App Store. We never see your card.</li>
      <li>We don't sell personal data or share it for advertising, and there are no ad pixels, advertising cookies or cross-site tracking on this website.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="app-store">3. The App Store copy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It makes no network requests. There is no key to check, and the App Store brings its updates.</li>
      <li>Apple handles the purchase, the payment and any refund. We get sales figures from Apple, not who you are. See <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li>It keeps its settings and paintings in its own sandbox, in <code>~/Library/Containers/app.outbound.Outbound</code>.</li>
      <li>Support, Feedback and Privacy in the app open this website in your browser, where <a href="#site">section 6</a> applies.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="direct">4. The copy from this website</h2>
    <h3>The license check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>When you buy from the app, it asks this website to start a checkout, then fetches your key once you've paid. The website keeps nothing about you.</li>
      <li>When you unlock Outbound, it sends your license key and your Mac's name to Polar, the store that sells it, so the key can count which Macs use it.</li>
      <li>About every two weeks it asks Polar whether the key is still active. Offline is fine for a month.</li>
      <li>Deactivating in Settings tells Polar to free that Mac's place.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Updates</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Once a day Outbound asks this website whether there is a new version, and downloads it from GitHub if there is. Nothing about you is sent beyond what any web request carries: your IP address, and the versions of Outbound and macOS.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="mac">5. What stays on your Mac</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your license key, in your keychain (the copy from this website only).</li>
      <li>Your settings, in the app's preferences.</li>
      <li>Paintings of the current view, used as your desktop picture, and a record of the desktop pictures they cover, so yours can be put back.</li>
      <li>Outbound reads where the cursor is so the bird can follow it. It never records it or sends it anywhere, and needs no special permission.</li>
      <li>None of this leaves your Mac. Quit Outbound and drag it to the Trash to remove it; its files are in <code>~/Library/Application Support/Outbound</code>, or in the sandbox above for the App Store copy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="site">6. This website</h2>
    <h3>Hosting</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>The website runs on Cloudflare, which receives your IP address, browser and the page asked for in order to deliver and protect it. We don't keep logs of visits ourselves. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li>It picks your language from your browser's settings, and your country from your IP address to show prices in your money. Neither is stored.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Counting visits</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Visits are counted with Plausible: which pages are seen, where visitors came from, and their country, browser and kind of device. It sets no cookies and keeps nothing that identifies you. On the thank-you page it gets only the page, not the checkout in its address. See <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy">Plausible's data policy</a>.</li>
      <li>It also counts clicks on Buy and Download, which questions in the FAQ are opened, and finished purchases with their price before tax, never who made them.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What this website keeps in your browser</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A <code>lang</code> cookie, for a year, only if you pick a language at the bottom of a page. It is sent back so the right language is shown, and does nothing else.</li>
      <li>After you buy, your key, for a year, so the homepage can show it if you lose it. It never leaves your browser. Click Forget to remove it.</li>
      <li>That you joined the waitlist and for which platform, and which order this browser has already counted, so neither is repeated. During a checkout, its id, in that tab only.</li>
      <li>Clearing this website's data in your browser removes all of it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="buying">7. Buying on this website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>On this website, Outbound is sold by Polar Software, Inc., our reseller and the merchant of record. Polar takes the payment, charges and pays the tax, sends your receipt and handles refunds. It collects your name, email address, billing address and payment details for that under <a href="https://polar.sh/legal/privacy-policy">Polar's privacy policy</a>. We never see or store card details.</li>
      <li>Polar gives us your email address, country, what you bought and what you paid, and keeps your license key and the Macs using it for us. We use them only to deliver your key, to help when you write, and for our records. We never sell them, or share them for any other purpose.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="waitlist">8. The waitlist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If you ask to hear when Outbound comes to Windows or iPhone, your email address is kept with the platform you picked, the page's language and the date. Nothing else is collected.</li>
      <li>It is stored with Supabase, which hosts the database, and is used for one email when that version is out. Then it's deleted. It is never shared or used for anything else. See <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy">Supabase's privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li>To be taken off sooner, email <a href="mailto:outbound@edbn.me">outbound@edbn.me</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="feedback">9. Feedback and email</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>What you write on the feedback page is kept with Supabase, with the page's language and the date. Opened from the app, it also notes the app's version, and how the painting runs on that Mac: its chip, macOS version and number of displays, what was holding the painting still, and how quickly the Mac's graphics paint it, with any error they gave.</li>
      <li>Your email address is kept only if you give it, and only used to reply.</li>
      <li>Email you send to outbound@edbn.me is forwarded by Cloudflare to our mailbox, and kept as long as it helps to answer you.</li>
      <li>Feedback and email are read by the person who makes Outbound, and never shared. To have them deleted, ask.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="why">10. Why we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>To deliver what you bought</strong>, and to support it: your order, key, Macs and messages. This is needed to perform our contract with you.</li>
      <li><strong>To run and protect the website and count visits</strong>, in ways that don't identify you to us. These are our legitimate interests, and you can object to them.</li>
      <li><strong>To email you about Windows or iPhone, or reply to feedback</strong>, because you asked us to. You can withdraw that at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>To keep records the law requires</strong>, such as tax records, which Polar and Apple keep as the sellers of record.</li>
      <li>We make no automated decisions about you that have legal or similar effects, and build no profiles.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="who-else">11. Who else handles it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, security and email forwarding for this website.</li>
      <li><strong>Polar</strong>: our reseller for purchases on this website. It handles payments, tax, receipts and refunds as the seller, and keeps license keys for us. See <a href="https://polar.sh/legal/privacy-policy">Polar's privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Apple</strong>: purchases, updates and refunds for the App Store copy.</li>
      <li><strong>Plausible</strong>: counting visits, without cookies or personal data.</li>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong>: the database for the waitlist and feedback.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub</strong>: hosting the downloads and the source code. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</li>
      <li>We share personal data only with these services, only for these purposes, and otherwise only when the law requires it or to protect our rights. If Outbound is ever sold, it would pass to the new owner under this policy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="transfers">12. International transfers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We are based in India, and the services above work in many countries, including the United States. Your personal data may be handled outside the country where you live.</li>
      <li>Where the GDPR, UK GDPR or Swiss law requires it, those transfers rely on an adequacy decision, such as the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework where a service is certified, or on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses in the services' data processing terms.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how-long">13. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Orders, receipts and keys: as long as Polar or Apple must keep them for tax and accounting, usually several years.</li>
      <li>The waitlist: until the one email is sent, then deleted.</li>
      <li>Feedback and email: as long as they help to answer you or improve Outbound, and deleted sooner when you ask.</li>
      <li>Visit counts: Plausible keeps only totals, which identify no one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="security">14. Security</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Everything travels over HTTPS. The website sends a strict Content Security Policy and other security headers, and its tokens for Polar and Supabase are kept as secrets that can do only what the website needs.</li>
      <li>On your Mac, the license key is kept in your keychain.</li>
      <li>No system is perfectly secure. If a breach ever put your personal data at risk, we would tell you and the authorities as the law requires.</li>
      <li>To report a security problem, email <a href="mailto:outbound@edbn.me">outbound@edbn.me</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="rights">15. Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Depending on where you live, you can ask to see the personal data we hold about you, to correct it, to delete it, to receive it in a portable form, to restrict or object to how we use it, and to withdraw consent you gave. We won't treat you differently for asking.</li>
      <li><strong>EEA, UK and Switzerland</strong>: you can also complain to your data protection authority.</li>
      <li><strong>United States</strong>: we don't sell personal data or share it for targeted advertising.</li>
      <li><strong>India</strong>: under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask for a summary of your data and how it is used, have it corrected or erased, nominate someone to act for you, and raise a grievance with us. If you aren't satisfied, you can approach the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
      <li>Email <a href="mailto:outbound@edbn.me">outbound@edbn.me</a> from the address you used, and we'll answer within a month, or sooner where the law requires. For purchases, Polar or Apple may need to act too, and we'll help.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="children">16. Children</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Outbound and this website aren't directed to children under 13, or under 16 in the EEA and UK, and we don't knowingly collect their personal data. If you think a child has given us some, email us and we'll delete it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="changes">17. Changes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>If this policy changes, the new version will be here with a new date at the top. If a change matters, we'll say so on this page before it takes effect.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="contact">18. Contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Questions, requests and complaints: <a href="mailto:outbound@edbn.me">outbound@edbn.me</a>.</li>
      <li>See also the <a href="/terms">Terms</a> and the <a href="/license">License</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
